{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>It is the sin-offering of the congregation.</b> The word הוא refers back to the bull. And it is possible to interpret that in its totality it comes to allude that in it was the sin of the congregation of Israel in the wilderness, according to the statement of the Sages, blessed be their memory, that they dropped one of the טטרמולין of the Chariot, as it says (Ezekiel 1:10): ״ופני שור מהשמאל לארבעתם״." "<b>And behold,</b> the offerings in the case of the anointed priest and the congregation are identical, for thus Aaron began to make it and Israel went astray after him; and it is written (Exodus 32:35): ״את העגל אשר עשו״ — the calf which they made; ״את העגל אשר עשה אהרן״ — the calf which Aaron made." "<b>And you should be roused</b> to consider further how Scripture mentioned above, in the case of the bull of the anointed priest, ״תמים לה׳״ — 'perfect for YHWH' — but did not so mention it here, in the case of the bull of the congregation. For regarding the bull of the anointed priest it says: ״פר בן בקר תמים לה׳ לחטאת״, while here it says: ״והקריבו הקהל פר בן בקר לחטאת״, and did not mention in it תמים. And all this is to allude that Aaron's intention was perfect for YHWH, as in his statement ״חג לה׳ מחר״, whereas among the congregation there was one whose heart was not perfect for YHWH, for some of them asked it as a leader and some of them made of it a god, as in the manner of what is written: ״וישתחוו לו ויזבחו לו״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:52.344577010Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}